      "writtenOn": "2024-05-28T15:48:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My one issue with the term `obfuscated` is that we want this for any target that is optimized *or* obfuscated. @rahulrav@google.com @christofferqa@google.com do y\u0027all have any thoughts on naming relative to the terminology we use elsewhere (in AGP)? Was looking at upstream documentation (https://developer.android.com/topic/performance/baselineprofiles/overview) and there\u0027s not really a clear naming distinction between rewritten/optimized baseline profiles and \"pre\"-rewritten baseline profiles. Would be OK with `unoptimized_profile`, `is_profile_unoptimized`, or possibly something a bit more explicit like `enable_profile_rewriting* bool` or `rewrite_profile_with_optimization* bool` or something like that.\n\nDon\u0027t feel strongly about a separate profile path or a flag as long as soong fails if you try to configure something ambiguous.",
      "parentUuid": "ed49a5c4_dafa95c9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 169,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 169,
        "endChar": 18
      },
